{"id": "unknown-2026-11-28-004", "date": "2026-11-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.17, "keywords": ["growth", "improve", "slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indonesia needs stronger productivity to meet 2045 income target: OECD", "content": "Indonesia needs annual growth of 5.8 per cent to achieve high-income status by 2045, but productivity constraints could slow growth to 3.5 per cent, the OECD said. \nIt recommended trade and investment reforms, stronger skills, greater female workforce participation and improved governance. \nThe OECD projects GDP growth of 5.4 per cent in 2026 and 5.3 per cent in 2027 and 2028.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indonesia-needs-stronger-productivity-to-meet-2045-income-target-oecd-315352-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
